CHAPTER.VERS:
And it came to pass, as the camels had finished drinking, that the man took a golden earring of half a shekel weight, and two bracelets for her wrists of ten
weight of gold;
earring: or, jewel for the forehead

Behold, I stand by the well of water; and it shall come to pass, that when the virgin cometh forth to draw 
        , and I say to her, Give me, I pray thee, a little 
        water of thy pitcher to drink;
